@spec keyDispatch_spec  src=tests/specs/keyDispatch_spec.lua  loc=411  cases=18
@exercises keyQueue (kq), commandManager (cmgr), keyDispatch (kd)
@surface   kq:fill, cmgr:registerAll, cmgr:bind, kd.dispatchKeys, cmgr:scope, cmgr:push, cmgr:pop, cmgr:letterCapture, cmgr:beginPrefix, kq:take, cmgr:isPrefixActive, cmgr:finishPrefix, kq:takeAny

# Intent
  keyDispatch: the prefix-capture + keychain walk extracted from coordinator
  (design/fx-patterns.md P3 step a). Now an importable module the fx-pattern
  mini modal reuses, so pin the dispatch contract directly: first-hit claiming,
  commandHeld hold-tracking, the acceptCmds gate, prefix capture + finish,
  false-declines, and the pageSuppressed root narrowing.
  
  The dispatcher is handed a real keyQueue, filled from the same fake ImGui each
  time a test sets the key state (see docs/keyQueue.md). Every reader in it takes
  what it acts on, so the queue after the pass is the observable throughout: a
  press something fired on is gone, one nothing acted on is still there, and a
  declined one is back. The pass returns commandHeld alone -- the keys down and
  command-bound at the live chord, which note entry consults per key -- and which
  dispatch may claim at all while one of the four owners holds the frame.

# Helpers
  @fn setKeys(opts)  @ 36-41
      -- A pressed key is also down; `down` alone models a hold with no fresh press. `owner`
      -- names one of the four keyboard owners the fill records, or nobody.
  @fn loadKD()  @ 48-55
      -- Rebind imgui to ours before loading keyDispatch: earlier specs' module-load
      -- preloads cache a different fake, so nil both and re-require (curveEditor idiom).
      -- keyQueue enumerates the shim it finds, so instantiate it under the same rebind.
  @fn freshCmgr()  @ 59-73
      -- Fresh real cmgr with commands bound to bare (Mod_None) keys; the returned log
      -- records which bodies ran and the last prefix arg one received.

# Cases
  @case 'a scope capturing letters takes them ahead of the keychain walk'  [pure]  @ 81-103
  @case 'a captured letter is reported held, so the same frame\'s note entry skips it'  [pure]  @ 110-123
  @case 'a slash during prefix entry appends and opens the walk; a digit takes it back'  [pure]  @ 131-155
  @case 'a letter after the slash walks, and leaves the prefix for the leaf to freeze'  [pure]  @ 162-182
  @case 'a pressed bound key fires its command, is claimed, and reports as held'  [pure]  @ 186-195
  @case 'the press is claimed before the command it selects runs'  [pure]  @ 202-217
  @case 'acceptCmds=false short-circuits: nothing dispatched'  [pure]  @ 221-229
  @case 'a held (not freshly pressed) bound key reports in commandHeld but does not fire'  [pure]  @ 233-242
  @case 'a digit while a prefix is open is captured, not dispatched'  [pure]  @ 246-256
  @case 'with a prefix open, a bound key freezes the prefix, dispatches, and clears it'  [pure]  @ 260-271
  @case 'a command returning false declines, and its press goes back in the queue'  [pure]  @ 278-289
  @case 'pageSuppressed narrows the walk to root: page bindings die, globals live'  [pure]  @ 293-314
  @case 'a shift-chord binding fires under shift and reports held'  [pure]  @ 318-329
  @case 'the same key pressed bare ignores the shift binding entirely'  [pure]  @ 333-344
  @case 'held marking follows the live chord: bare binding unmarked while shift is down'  [pure]  @ 348-356
  @case 'a captured digit leaves the queue; the press nothing claimed stays in it'  [pure]  @ 363-372
  @case 'a captured letter leaves the queue, at the mask it was struck with'  [pure]  @ 378-389
  @case 'under an owner, only the dispatch claiming that name captures'  [pure]  @ 396-409

